(version 1)

# Carried over from the Space Bug (legacy/gnss-px1105r-18mm-highpower-ext-ant), whose front end this board reuses.
# The RF class stays at 0.2 mm: that gap to the ground pour sets the 50 ohm coplanar line, so it is load-bearing.
#
# V2: the LNAs are SOT-23-6 (U3 AT2659S, U4 MAX2640) at 0.95 mm pitch, so V1's TSNP-6 fan-out rule is gone.

# PX100 (U1) is QFN-40 at 0.4 mm pitch with 0.22 mm lands: 0.18 mm between pads. V3 copies the Tinker-Beetle V2's GNSS
# layout and its rule: RF-class copper (LNA_IN1/LNA_IN2, pins 40/37) may come within 0.15 mm of other copper inside
# U1's courtyard; everything else keeps the default clearance.
(rule "PX100 QFN-40 RF pin fan-out"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.Type != 'Zone' && B.Type != 'Zone' && (A.NetClass == 'RF' || B.NetClass == 'RF') && A.intersectsCourtyard('U1') && B.intersectsCourtyard('U1')"))
